.TH MD_GET_THREAD_COUNT 3 "2026-10-17" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_thread_count \- query the resolved channel processing thread budget
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

size_t md_get_thread_count(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return the maximum number of processing participants, including the caller.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle, or NULL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The resolved budget, or zero for NULL. One means serial processing. This is
not the number of threads currently executing; small workloads use fewer
participants. The budget is fixed for the handle's lifetime.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls accessing the same handle, including queries.
.SH VERSION
Available in the libmorsedec 0.2.0 development API, shared-library ABI 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR md_new_with_threads (3),
.BR md_new_iq_with_threads (3),
.BR libmorsedec (3)
